  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovation Window: Introducing new e-cooking solutions in Eastern DRC suburban areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project pilots e-cooking distribution in the Democratic Republic of Congo DRC by applying two different approaches and involving two key partners: (1)	500 induction hobs (single or dual-burner) will be directly purchased and sold by the energy utility to households (HHs) that will pay upfront a little part of the price (that will be discounted through Demand side subsidies offered by the project) while the remaining value will be paid in instalment through the electricity bill; (2)	240 induction hobs will be sold by one or more distributors/retailers (third parties) recommended by another energy utility.</narrative>
  </description>
